-- UNIVERSAL1 - ALL SQL OF A FRESH DATABASE IN ONE FILE: kit8/sql/run_fresh_data.sql
-- GENERATED by kit8/sql/tools/build_run_fresh_data.js from the files of kit8/sql/init - do not edit here, edit those files and run the script again.
--
-- Supabase -> SQL Editor -> paste this whole file -> Run. Every part is idempotent and non-destructive (CREATE ... IF NOT EXISTS, seeds ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING),
-- so it is safe to run twice. Order and what each part adds:
--
--    1. done/create_tables.sql
--       base tables, personTable, contractTable, the PM project / task tables, kit8_setup_def_table, pm_touch_updated_at, pm_owns_project
--    2. update_currency_exchange_rate_types.sql
--       exchange rate TYPES (Default | Budget, as D365 FO): the key of a rate = day or day|Type
--    3. insert_currency_exchange_rates_2025_2026.sql
--       ECB exchange rates 2025 -> 2026 (Default: every working day, Budget: the planned rate of the year) for 9 currencies; generated by build_currency_rates_sql.js
--    4. create_product_tables.sql
--       product catalog + the shared descriptor / variant / price tables
--    5. create_resource_role_tables.sql
--       role types, roles, role rates, descriptors seniority / workLanguage / certification
--    6. create_management_genus_table.sql
--       management genus: costs (time / material / expense), revenue, payments
--    7. insert_rows_resource_table.sql
--       demo human / material / expense / revenue roles; managementGenus on the role types
--    8. create_person_type_table.sql
--       personTypeTable (Employee, Contractor) + 50 % Employee / 50 % Contractor of all persons
--    9. create_person_descriptors.sql
--       person Properties + Variants (separate certificate rows), a contract for every person
--   10. create_template_resource_contract_table.sql
--       templateResourceContractTable (rowOwnerGUID = management genus) + demo templates
--   11. create_pm_task_line_table.sql
--       task_line_table + RPC pm_set_task_last_edit_place (rowJSON.lastEditPlace)
--   12. create_user_calendar_tables.sql
--       user calendars, events, reminders
--
-- The delete scripts are in it too, as the RESET section right below this header - COMMENTED OUT, so nothing is deleted unless you remove the "-- " signs.
--
-- NOT in this file, on purpose (everything a fresh database needs is already in the parts above):
--   update_prices.sql, update_product_units.sql, update_product_vat.sql, rename_product_package_table.sql
--                                     migrations of an OLDER database - create_product_tables.sql already creates the same result; update_product_vat.sql would
--                                     also overwrite the VAT you set by hand on every run, update_product_units.sql / rename_* contain guarded DROP / RENAME
--   create_prices_for_all_products_and_variants.sql
--                                     ~3100 demo prices: the dashboard reads 1000 rows per table, so it would show the prices only in part (run it by hand if wanted)
--   create_task_expense_input_table.sql  obsolete (the table of a removed demo)
